WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:02.735
-I got to say, congrats
on this film, "Uncut Gems."

00:00:02.735 --> 00:00:04.871
-Thank you, pal.
-It's unbelievable.

00:00:04.871 --> 00:00:06.739
It's getting insane reviews.

00:00:06.739 --> 00:00:10.176
"Sandler's supernova presence
radiates." -- "Variety."

00:00:10.176 --> 00:00:11.410
-Yes.
-Some say,

00:00:11.410 --> 00:00:12.978
"It's a hell of a part.
And Sandler aces it."

00:00:12.978 --> 00:00:14.914
"A career high."
I mean, there's --

00:00:14.914 --> 00:00:17.083
It's getting Oscar buzz. And --
-Yeah.

00:00:17.083 --> 00:00:19.719
-How's that feel? I want to ask
you, like, are you, like,

00:00:19.719 --> 00:00:21.320
did you ever think you would
get Oscar buzz?

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:23.789
-No.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:23.789 --> 00:00:27.260
No, no, no.
I think when I was young,

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:29.862
I thought "Billy Madison"
or something had a shot.

00:00:29.862 --> 00:00:32.298
[ Laughter ]
And then I -- But they --

00:00:32.298 --> 00:00:35.401
They took that away from me.
So I stopped dreaming.

00:00:35.401 --> 00:00:37.069
Yeah.
-Yeah. Who --

00:00:37.069 --> 00:00:38.704
The directors are
the Safdie brothers?

00:00:38.704 --> 00:00:41.073
-Safdie brothers.
Two great guys. Josh and Benny.

00:00:41.073 --> 00:00:42.976
Man, are they good.
-God, this --

00:00:42.976 --> 00:00:45.278
I saw their movie "Good Time."
-Yeah, yes.

00:00:45.278 --> 00:00:46.912
-Robert Pattinson.
And I just saw that movie.

00:00:46.912 --> 00:00:48.681
And I go, "Ooh."
And it put a knot in my stomach.

00:00:48.681 --> 00:00:50.916
-Oh, me too. Me too.
-So I was excited that

00:00:50.916 --> 00:00:52.418
you were working
with these guys.

00:00:52.418 --> 00:00:53.986
-Yeah.
-And doing a dramatic role.

00:00:53.986 --> 00:00:55.888
So I was sitting here.
This is a true story.

00:00:55.888 --> 00:00:57.089
I was talking to Lorne.
-Yeah.

00:00:57.089 --> 00:00:58.391
-Lorne Michaels who --
-Yes.

00:00:58.391 --> 00:01:00.927
-And he says, "I'm going to
go see Adam's movies."

00:01:00.927 --> 00:01:02.261
-Right, right.
-Some big film --

00:01:02.261 --> 00:01:03.329
New York Film Festival thing.

00:01:03.329 --> 00:01:04.797
You're a part of this
film festival.

00:01:04.797 --> 00:01:06.833
So I go, "Great. I'll go."
I go, "I have a double taping.

00:01:06.833 --> 00:01:08.101
It'll be great."
He goes,

00:01:08.101 --> 00:01:09.402
"All right, I'll see you there."
I go, "no problem."

00:01:09.402 --> 00:01:11.271
He goes, "You going?"
I go, "Yeah, I can't wait."

00:01:11.271 --> 00:01:12.271
I go, "You waiting for me?"

00:01:12.271 --> 00:01:13.706
He goes,
"No, I'll meet you there."

00:01:13.706 --> 00:01:15.575
"Okay, great." So he goes.
Lorne goes ahead of me.

00:01:15.575 --> 00:01:17.210
I do -- I double tape
the show that night.

00:01:17.210 --> 00:01:18.911
I get in the car.
I go down to Lincoln Center.

00:01:18.911 --> 00:01:20.379
Go down this big theater,
I go down.

00:01:20.379 --> 00:01:21.914
Someone brings me down.
Open the doors.

00:01:21.914 --> 00:01:25.418
Giant theater full of people.
And I look for Lorne.

00:01:25.418 --> 00:01:27.319
They -- I see Lorne's
in the middle of the row

00:01:27.319 --> 00:01:29.588
with Chris Rock and Ben Stiller.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:29.588 --> 00:01:31.424
[ Light laughter ]
-No room for me.

00:01:31.424 --> 00:01:33.226
No seat saved at all.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:33.226 --> 00:01:35.094
Nothing. I go,
"What -- guy, I mean,

00:01:35.094 --> 00:01:36.829
didn't we have a thing?
I mean, what's going on?"

00:01:36.829 --> 00:01:38.364
So I go, "Hey, what's up."
And then I go,

00:01:38.364 --> 00:01:39.698
"All right,
I guess I'll just sit."

00:01:39.698 --> 00:01:41.233
So I sat at the end of the row
by myself.

00:01:41.233 --> 00:01:42.435
-Yes, yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:42.435 --> 00:01:43.969
-And so I was there
next to woman.

00:01:43.969 --> 00:01:45.271
-Yeah.
-And I said,

00:01:45.271 --> 00:01:47.106
"Hi, nice to see you.
I'm very excited about this.

00:01:47.106 --> 00:01:49.542
I'm a big -- So I'm,
like, getting ready for the --

00:01:49.542 --> 00:01:50.810
-Small talking.
-Yeah.

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:52.878
-Yeah.
-So then the movie's

00:01:52.878 --> 00:01:55.148
about to start.
The lights go down a little bit.

00:01:55.148 --> 00:01:56.616
And this woman stands up.
And she leaves.

00:01:56.616 --> 00:01:59.652
There's an empty seat. And who
sits in the seat next to me?

00:01:59.652 --> 00:02:01.920
Adam Sandler.
-That's right, baby.

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:04.624
[ Cheers and applause ]
I saw you. I saw you.

00:02:04.624 --> 00:02:07.092
-The Sand man.
The Sand man came in!

00:02:07.092 --> 00:02:09.928
-I saw that his little heart
broken eyes,

00:02:09.928 --> 00:02:11.330
"Nobody loves me."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:11.330 --> 00:02:14.167
And daddy showed up.
And then --

00:02:14.167 --> 00:02:16.135
Can I tell them
what you did to me?

00:02:16.135 --> 00:02:17.670
-Yeah, sure.

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:19.606
-He pulled the popcorn trick
on me.

00:02:19.606 --> 00:02:21.340
[ Laughter ]

00:02:21.340 --> 00:02:23.976
I couldn't believe it.
Jimmy, when you --

00:02:23.976 --> 00:02:27.180
-No, no, no, no.
-And it was the best popcorn

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:31.083
I've ever eaten in my life.
-But it -- no.

00:02:31.083 --> 00:02:33.419
How was I as a seat mate?

00:02:33.419 --> 00:02:36.689
As a seat mate,
how was I though?

00:02:36.689 --> 00:02:39.291
-You were the best guy
to watch this movie with.

00:02:39.291 --> 00:02:42.061
By the way, you know Jimmy's
enthusiasm is incredible.

00:02:42.061 --> 00:02:44.464
And he --
If you sit next to Jimmy,

00:02:44.464 --> 00:02:46.432
and you have a movie coming out,

00:02:46.432 --> 00:02:50.269
he is the proper man to make you
think that you did a great job.

00:02:50.269 --> 00:02:53.005
[ Laughter ]
Because you were so --

00:02:53.005 --> 00:02:56.875
This movie is very, like, it
gets you a little upset.

00:02:56.875 --> 00:02:58.311
And you're nervous
throughout the thing.

00:02:58.311 --> 00:03:00.346
Jimmy was so nervous
and so excited.

00:03:00.346 --> 00:03:04.250
And every line I said,
I'm watching the movie.

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:06.219
You know,
I don't love watching myself.

00:03:06.219 --> 00:03:07.920
But Jimmy would grab me
and be like,

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:09.488
"Oh, my God, I loved that."
And I'd be like,

00:03:09.488 --> 00:03:11.824
"Yeah, yeah. That's right.
It was good, wasn't it?"

00:03:11.824 --> 00:03:12.858
[ Laughter ]
Yeah,

00:03:12.858 --> 00:03:14.260
you made me feel top there,
buddy.

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:16.095
-I honestly --
that was one of these movies

00:03:16.095 --> 00:03:18.130
I couldn't believe it.
First of all, after, like,

00:03:18.130 --> 00:03:21.800
I want to say, five minutes into
it, I don't see you anymore.

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:23.769
I see this character
that you're playing.

00:03:23.769 --> 00:03:25.671
-That's great.
-Is it Harvey or Howard?

00:03:25.671 --> 00:03:26.772
-Howard.
-Howard.

00:03:26.772 --> 00:03:28.107
-Howard Ratner. Yes, yes.
-Howard Ratner.

00:03:28.107 --> 00:03:29.641
-I looked different.
I dress different.

00:03:29.641 --> 00:03:31.644
-You talk differently.
And everything -- and, like --

00:03:31.644 --> 00:03:33.980
I just feel bad
for this guy, man.

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:36.582
-Oh, yeah.
-And he's kind of a gambler.

00:03:36.582 --> 00:03:38.317
And he works in
the diamond district.

00:03:38.317 --> 00:03:39.652
-Yes.
-Which is right here

00:03:39.652 --> 00:03:41.153
on 47th Street.
-Yes, yes, yes.

00:03:41.153 --> 00:03:43.222
-Did you get to hang out
and meet those guys?

00:03:43.222 --> 00:03:44.524
-I got to -- sure.
I mean,

00:03:44.524 --> 00:03:46.125
I did research
for the character.

00:03:46.125 --> 00:03:47.860
The Safdie brothers
brought me there.

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:49.762
And I got to know everybody
on the block.

00:03:49.762 --> 00:03:51.664
And they all let me
in their lives.

00:03:51.664 --> 00:03:53.732
And allowed me
to work with them and --

00:03:53.732 --> 00:03:56.368
you know, I didn't do any work.
But I watched them work.

00:03:56.368 --> 00:03:58.338
[ Laughter ] And they taught me
about jewelry.

00:03:58.338 --> 00:04:00.173
And they taught me about how
they do sales.

00:04:00.173 --> 00:04:01.841
-But it's a tight knit
family that --

00:04:01.841 --> 00:04:04.077
-Yes, nobody get's in there.
-It's a little area. No.

00:04:04.077 --> 00:04:05.244
-It really is a cool block.

00:04:05.244 --> 00:04:06.879
It's amazing when you go there.

00:04:06.879 --> 00:04:08.747
It's just been the same
for so long.

00:04:08.747 --> 00:04:11.217
And they just --
It's family business.

00:04:11.217 --> 00:04:14.153
And they -- They taught me a
lot.

00:04:14.153 --> 00:04:17.790
And I did -- this is --
if I can -- they --

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:20.359
I couldn't let the character go.

00:04:20.359 --> 00:04:22.328
They gave me a loop.
They gave me a loop.

00:04:22.328 --> 00:04:24.630
So when I shot the movie,
I was so in --

00:04:24.630 --> 00:04:26.698
excited about getting to know
jewelry and stuff.

00:04:26.698 --> 00:04:28.367
And they gave me one of --
you know the loop thing?

00:04:28.367 --> 00:04:30.303
-That magnifies the --
-That magnifies the thing.

00:04:30.303 --> 00:04:33.339
And so, yeah. I started
looking at everybody's jewelry

00:04:33.339 --> 00:04:35.241
to see if it was good or bad.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:35.241 --> 00:04:37.510
And then -- this is the weirdest
thing I discovered.

00:04:37.510 --> 00:04:39.645
Because of the loop,
I have a penis.

00:04:39.645 --> 00:04:41.614
I had no idea.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:41.614 --> 00:04:43.650
I was so excited.
-Congratulations!

00:04:43.650 --> 00:04:45.017
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah, yeah.

00:04:45.017 --> 00:04:46.252
-Congratulations.
-It felt cool.

00:04:46.252 --> 00:04:48.454
-That's awesome.
Yeah, that's fantastic.

00:04:48.454 --> 00:04:51.857
-Thank you.
And, guys, it's also uncut.

00:04:51.857 --> 00:04:56.829
[ Laughter ]
But I have to report to you,

00:04:56.829 --> 00:04:58.798
sadly, it's not a gem.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:58.798 --> 00:05:04.203
It was trying, though.
-Oh, my gosh.

00:05:04.203 --> 00:05:05.438
So I'm watching this thing.

00:05:05.438 --> 00:05:07.273
And there are some funny scenes
in it.

00:05:07.273 --> 00:05:08.907
-Yes.
-You have some good things.

00:05:08.907 --> 00:05:10.843
But it is really riveting.
And seriously,

00:05:10.843 --> 00:05:13.713
there is a knot in your stomach.
And I'm watching your character.

00:05:13.713 --> 00:05:15.647
And I'm like,
"Oh, just don't do it man."

00:05:15.647 --> 00:05:17.349
Just like,
"Oh, just go home, dude.

00:05:17.349 --> 00:05:19.851
Just go home. Just stop.
What are you doing?"

00:05:19.851 --> 00:05:22.154
And you just push it.
And these directors are great.

00:05:22.154 --> 00:05:23.923
-Yeah. Oh, yeah.
-The soundtrack is killer.

00:05:23.923 --> 00:05:25.825
-Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah.
-And it just gets better

00:05:25.825 --> 00:05:28.161
and crazier and just awesomer.
And now -- and the ending --

00:05:28.161 --> 00:05:29.795
I don't want to tell anybody.
But it was so --

00:05:29.795 --> 00:05:31.030
but anyways -- I'm happy.
-Yes.

00:05:31.030 --> 00:05:32.164
-Last five minutes of the movie,

00:05:32.164 --> 00:05:33.432
you had to leave to go do
a Q&amp;A.

00:05:33.432 --> 00:05:35.101
-I know. I went --
I had to leave you. But --

00:05:35.101 --> 00:05:36.702
-I'm happy you did.
-I know. I know.

00:05:36.702 --> 00:05:38.171
-'Cause I loved --
-We had --

00:05:38.171 --> 00:05:39.905
We went to the party after,
though.

00:05:39.905 --> 00:05:41.607
-Yeah, what a great party
that was.

00:05:41.607 --> 00:05:43.543
-They had a party
at Katz's Delicatessen.

00:05:43.543 --> 00:05:45.678
-It was great.
-And everybody was, like,

00:05:45.678 --> 00:05:47.914
so funny.
Usually at a party after a movie

00:05:47.914 --> 00:05:49.781
is a drink and celebration.

00:05:49.781 --> 00:05:51.751
This was just people eating
corned beef sandwiches.

00:05:51.751 --> 00:05:55.154
[ Laughter ]
-Biz Markie was deejaying.

00:05:55.154 --> 00:05:56.889
-Biz Markie was incredible.
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:05:56.889 --> 00:05:58.424
-It was great.
It was such a fun party.

00:05:58.424 --> 00:06:00.059
-It was fun.
-And I got to meet these guys

00:06:00.059 --> 00:06:01.727
from the film that are, like,
real people.

00:06:01.727 --> 00:06:03.128
-Oh, yes, yes.
-They're not actors.

00:06:03.128 --> 00:06:04.697
They're kind of characters
in real life.

00:06:04.697 --> 00:06:06.165
-They're characters, yeah,
yeah.

00:06:06.165 --> 00:06:08.367
They're a lot of the people from
the jewelry district are in it.

00:06:08.367 --> 00:06:12.171
And then there are some guys
after me in the movie who are --

00:06:12.171 --> 00:06:17.376
the Safdie brothers are really
into the right cast

00:06:17.376 --> 00:06:18.777
and who has the right look.

00:06:18.777 --> 00:06:20.680
And there are all these --
a lot of them weren't actors.

00:06:20.680 --> 00:06:22.382
And these guys who beat me up
in the --

00:06:22.382 --> 00:06:24.116
I get beat up throughout
the movie a lot

00:06:24.116 --> 00:06:25.618
'cause I owe money and stuff.

00:06:25.618 --> 00:06:29.822
But these guys who were beating
me up were really good guys.

00:06:29.822 --> 00:06:33.626
But they didn't ever do
a movie before.

00:06:33.626 --> 00:06:35.628
So there was a stunt coordinator
who would say, like,

00:06:35.628 --> 00:06:37.864
"You know, you don't
have to really choke at him."

00:06:37.864 --> 00:06:39.999
[ Laughter ]

00:06:39.999 --> 00:06:42.134
You know, it was like --
and then they were all like,

00:06:42.134 --> 00:06:43.435
"Yes." Nodding along nice.

00:06:43.435 --> 00:06:45.471
And, like, "You know, this looks
like you're choking him."

00:06:45.471 --> 00:06:47.740
And they were like -- They
literally didn't hear anything

00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:49.174
the guy was saying.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:49.174 --> 00:06:51.010
And they would talk to me like
they love me.

00:06:51.010 --> 00:06:52.911
Say like, "'Mr. Deeds' was
incredible."

00:06:52.911 --> 00:06:55.547
I was like, "Oh, thanks, man."
And then, "Action!"

00:06:55.547 --> 00:06:57.282
And then just full choke.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:57.282 --> 00:06:59.118
And I was, like,
trying to tap out.

00:06:59.118 --> 00:07:01.187
I'm punching the roof.
And they're like,

00:07:01.187 --> 00:07:02.855
"Adam's in character."
And I was like,

00:07:02.855 --> 00:07:04.924
"No, I really am getting
choked right now."

00:07:04.924 --> 00:07:08.293
[ Laughter ]
-It is unbelievable.

00:07:08.293 --> 00:07:10.829
And I just -- I gotta say,
dude, I just love seeing

00:07:10.829 --> 00:07:11.998
every single thing you do.

00:07:11.998 --> 00:07:13.432
I followed your career
through everything.

00:07:13.432 --> 00:07:15.367
But -- and the comedy special
was great you had this year.

00:07:15.367 --> 00:07:16.535
"SNL" was fantastic.
-Thanks.

00:07:16.535 --> 00:07:17.636
-You hosting -- that was great.

00:07:17.636 --> 00:07:19.071
-You being on there with me
was sweet.

00:07:19.071 --> 00:07:20.305
-No, that was great.
-Thank you.

00:07:20.305 --> 00:07:21.340
-But this thing is like --

00:07:21.340 --> 00:07:22.808
Dude, you deserve all the praise
for this.

00:07:22.808 --> 00:07:23.842
-Thanks, buddy.

00:07:23.842 --> 00:07:24.877
-"Uncut Gems."
Adam Sandler, everybody.

